# Grok Build 0.1 — SELF-EXCLUDED from scored findings (Step 5 Preview)

- Source: xAI / SpaceXAI (`grok-build-0.1`)
- Date: 2026-10-09 (UTC)
- Reason for exclusion: **zero verified public benchmarks exist for this model** — xAI published no evaluation table at launch and no independent tracker lists scores. No scored findings file was written; the roster entry carries a placeholder Overall.

## What is verified about the model

- xAI's fast, purpose-built agentic **coding** model — the engine behind the Grok Build CLI (terminal TUI, headless/CI mode, Agent Client Protocol integration; open-source Rust harness at xai-org/grok-build). Launched in **public beta 2026-05-20** (API announcement 2026-05-29), succeeding Grok Code Fast 1 as the flagship of the Grok Code line. API-only, proprietary, no weights.
- Specs: **256K context window**, **text + image in → text out** (reads diagrams, mockups, error screenshots), always-on reasoning that is **not user-configurable**, function calling, structured outputs (JSON schema), native **MCP** support. 100+ tok/s. No stated max-output limit or knowledge cutoff.
- Pricing: **$1.00/M input, $2.00/M output, $0.20/M cached input** on the xAI API; also via OpenRouter (`x-ai/grok-build-0.1`) and Vercel AI Gateway. Regions us-east-1/us-west-2, ~37 RPS.
- Training claim: trained specifically for agentic coding tasks (web development, debugging, MCP) rather than chat; xAI says it performs best in agentic harnesses — Grok Build, Cursor, Hermes Agent, OpenClaw, Kilo Code, OpenCode. Up to 8 parallel agents with plan→search→build workflows and isolated Git-worktree subagents (harness features, not model benchmarks).
- Launch coverage (DevOps.com) evaluated it against Claude Code and Cursor qualitatively only — "price and parallelism may be enough to earn a place in multi-agent orchestration stacks — just not necessarily the top spot" — with no numeric scores.

## What is missing (why exclusion)

- No SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, LiveCodeBench, GPQA or Artificial Analysis score from xAI or any third party.
- No model card / technical report with evals; the launch post and docs are feature-level only.
- Knowledge cutoff and max output undisclosed.

## Re-score trigger

When xAI or an independent tracker publishes an evaluation table (SWE-bench Verified/Pro, Terminal-Bench, MCP Atlas, GDPval) or Artificial Analysis indexes the model, write a normal `Step_5_Preview.md` for this slug covering Tool use, Reasoning, Context window, Multimodal, Coding, Cost efficiency and Overall per the methodology.

